{ "explanation": "## What is a Radian?

A **radian** is the natural unit of angle measurement. Instead of dividing a circle into an arbitrary 360 degrees, radians ask: *how far around the circle have you actually traveled?*

**Definition:** An angle of **1 radian** is the angle formed when the arc length along a circle exactly **equals the circle's radius**.

### Key intuition
- Imagine wrapping the radius around the circumference like a measuring tape.
- Each time you lay down one full radius-length of arc, you've swept 1 radian.
- Since the full circumference is 2πr, you can fit exactly **2π ≈ 6.283** radius-lengths around the circle.

### Why it's natural
In radians, arc length, radius, and angle connect beautifully:

$$s = r\theta \quad\Rightarrow\quad \theta = \frac{s}{r}$$

The arc length is just *radius × angle*. That's also why calculus formulas like $\frac{d}{dx}\sin x = \cos x$ **only** work in radians — the unit is baked into the math.

### Common conversions
| Degrees | Radians |
|---|---|
| 360° | 2π |
| 180° | π |
| 90° | π/2 |
| 1 radian | ≈ 57.3° |

**The animation below** shows a unit circle (r = 1). Drag the slider to sweep the angle: the blue arc's length is measured in "radius-sticks" — you can watch how many fit, with 2π of them completing the full circle.", "manimCode": "const R = 2.2;
const center = [0, 0.3, 0];

// Circle
const circle = new Circle({ radius: R, color: WHITE });
circle.moveTo(center);
circle.setStrokeWidth(2.5);

// Radius line (rotating)
const radiusLine = new Polygon({ vertices: [center, [center[0] + R, center[1], 0]], color: YELLOW });
radiusLine.setStrokeWidth(4).setFillOpacity(0);

// Arc tracker
let theta = 1.0;

// Arc (as polygon vertices along the circle)
function arcPoints(t0, t1, n) {
  const pts = [];
  for (let i = 0; i <= n; i++) {
    const a = t0 + (t1 - t0) * i / n;
    pts.push([center[0] + R * Math.cos(a), center[1] + R * Math.sin(a), 0]);
  }
  return pts;
}

let arc = new Polygon({ vertices: arcPoints(0, theta, 120), color: BLUE_C });
arc.setStrokeWidth(7).setFillOpacity(0);

// Dot on circle
const dot = new Dot({ point: [center[0] + R, center[1], 0], color: YELLOW });

// "Radius sticks" laid along the arc — shows arc length in units of r
const sticks = new VGroup();
function rebuildSticks(t) {
  scene.remove(sticks);
  const items = [];
  let laid = 0;
  while (laid + 0.5 <= t && items.length < 7) {
    const a0 = laid;
    const a1 = laid + 1;
    const mid = (a0 + a1) / 2;
    // chord from a0 to a1, drawn slightly inside
    const p0 = [center[0] + (R - 0.18) * Math.cos(a0), center[1] + (R - 0.18) * Math.sin(a0), 0];
    const p1 = [center[0] + (R - 0.18) * Math.cos(a1), center[1] + (R - 0.18) * Math.sin(a1), 0];
    const tick = new Polygon({ vertices: [p0, p1], color: ORANGE });
    tick.setStrokeWidth(4).setFillOpacity(0);
    items.push(tick);
    // number label
    const lp = [center[0] + (R - 0.55) * Math.cos(mid), center[1] + (R - 0.55) * Math.sin(mid), 0];
    const num = new Text({ text: String(items.length), color: ORANGE, fontSize: 18 });
    num.moveTo(lp);
    items.push(num);
    laid = a1;
  }
  sticks.group = items;
  items.forEach(it => sticks.add(it));
  scene.add(sticks);
}

// Radius reference stick at bottom for comparison
const refStick = new Polygon({ vertices: [[center[0] - 1.4, -3.3, 0], [center[0] - 1.4 + R, -3.3, 0]], color: ORANGE });
refStick.setStrokeWidth(5).setFillOpacity(0);
const refLabel = new Text({ text: 'r = 1 radius length', color: ORANGE, fontSize: 18 });
refLabel.nextTo(refStick, DOWN, 0.15);

// Readout text (immutable — rebuild on change)
let readout = new Text({
  text: 'θ = 1.00 rad  =  57.3°   (arc length = 1.00 r)',
  color: WHITE, fontSize: 26
});
readout.moveTo([0, 3.5, 0]);

let formula = new MathTex({ latex: '\\theta = \\frac{s}{r} \\quad \\text{rad}' });
await formula.waitForRender();
formula.moveTo([4.7, 2.6, 0]);
formula.setColor(GOLD);

// Rebuild function
function rebuild() {
  scene.remove(arc);
  arc = new Polygon({ vertices: arcPoints(0, theta, 150), color: BLUE_C });
  arc.setStrokeWidth(7).setFillOpacity(0);
  scene.add(arc);
  dot.moveTo([center[0] + R * Math.cos(theta), center[1] + R * Math.sin(theta), 0]);
  radiusLine.setVertices([center, [center[0] + R * Math.cos(theta), center[1] + R * Math.sin(theta), 0]]);
  rebuildSticks(theta);
  const pos = readout.getCenter();
  scene.remove(readout);
  readout = new Text({
    text: 'θ = ' + theta.toFixed(2) + ' rad  =  ' + (theta * 180 / Math.PI).toFixed(1) + '°   (arc length = ' + theta.toFixed(2) + ' r)',
    color: WHITE, fontSize: 26
  });
  readout.moveTo(pos);
  scene.add(readout);
}

// Intro animation
scene.add(circle, refStick);
await scene.play(new Write(readout));
await scene.wait(0.4);
rebuild();

// Sweep through key angles: 1 rad, π/2, π, 2π
const stops = [1, Math.PI / 2, Math.PI, 2 * Math.PI];
for (const target of stops) {
  const start = theta;
  const steps = 60;
  for (let i = 1; i <= steps; i++) {
    theta = start + (target - start) * i / steps;
    rebuild();
    await scene.wait(0.016);
  }
  await scene.wait(0.8);
}

// Controls for exploration
const controls = new Controls(scene, { position: 'top-left', width: 260 });
controls.addSlider({
  label: 'Angle θ (radians)',
  min: 0, max: 6.2832, value: 2 * Math.PI, step: 0.01,
  onChange: (v) => { theta = v; rebuild(); }
});
controls.addButton({
  label: 'Set to exactly 1 radian',
  onClick: () => { theta = 1; rebuild(); }
});
controls.addButton({
  label: 'Full circle (2π rad)',
  onClick: () => { theta = 2 * Math.PI; rebuild(); }
});

await scene.wait(999999);" }

